## Tradeoffs

**Release now, blockers accepted:** auth F-1 exposes every account permanently on any
token leak (blast radius = all users, irreversible without a restart), and storage
F1/F2 turn routine disk-full or deploy-kill events into destroyed persistent state with
no recovery path. Monitoring cannot detect either safely, and mitigations (external
backups, forced rotation) would have to be *new* guarantees the layer does not provide.
**Delay:** bounded engineering cost — atomic temp-file + fsync + rename for F1/F2/F3,
and an `authenticate` that enforces expiry over a private store for F-1/F-3. Delay is
cheaper than accepting irreversible data and credential exposure.

